       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any protocol that uses ibuprofen at 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and the 1,600 mg single dose is also above the usual ceiling. The risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events are high enough that I want an independent check before this goes in.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg PO 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day), or a lower dose if you prefer. Give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Route it through pharmacy:** If a protocol exists, the pharmacist who reviewed it can enter or co-sign the order through your system's high-dose override. Either of you can add the protocol reference to the order note.\n\nI'm not doubting you personally. As an ordering assistant, I can't confirm this kind of exception, and a 2\u00d7 overdose is hard to reverse."
